    "post_rendered": "The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" > lie on the diagonals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\"  width=\"27\" height=\"13\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\"  width=\"29\" height=\"12\" >,</span> respectively, of a quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\"  width=\"57\" height=\"13\" > such that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/2/e82fc3d864feebb67513e08b3f70870062e82bb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AP}{AC} + \\frac{BQ}{BD} =1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" >.</span> The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" > meets the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"13\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > and <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Prove that the circumcircles of the triangles <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b562ad3c803c3cbe6f2b6e1bd160acd5fe5d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMP$\"  width=\"47\" height=\"13\" >,</span> <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c908d33b6d40c3718d7668f4fd482d1bc2e56823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BNQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" >,</span> <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/826f44eb393737b2f44dc69e17c5eb5101163d1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DMQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"16\" >,</span> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c1ec2673c51d25a8561f2f3486ec6ac52549d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CNP$\"  width=\"45\" height=\"12\" > are concurrent.",
